00:31:59.790 --> 00:32:03.470
A senior prison official told me months ago that there have been

00:32:03.470 --> 00:32:08.670
active discussions about putting me in diesel therapy for the rest of my sentence.

00:32:08.670 --> 00:32:14.350
Diesel therapy is when a prisoner is transferred from one prison to another all across the country

00:32:14.350 --> 00:32:20.990
via prison van, bus, or con-air plane, never staying in any one prison long enough to receive

00:32:20.990 --> 00:32:26.990
telephone, email, mailing, or visitation privileges. I could move to a different prison

00:32:26.990 --> 00:32:31.150
every week for the rest of my sentence and still not hit them all. In the meantime,

00:32:31.150 --> 00:32:36.110
my family and attorneys wouldn't even know what time zone I was in. This would obviously be

00:32:36.110 --> 00:32:41.150
retaliation for letters from Loretto and my press interviews, but the BOP could easily

00:32:41.150 --> 00:32:47.070
make up a lie that it was related to a bed space issue or perhaps for my own safety.

00:32:48.030 --> 00:32:53.310
Still, it would stink of retaliation for the exercise of my constitutional right to freedom of

00:32:53.310 --> 00:32:58.910
speech. I'm fortunate that my attorneys, among Washington's best, are willing to sue individual

00:32:58.910 --> 00:33:04.670
BOP employees as well as the BOP as an organization to ensure that such an assault on my rights

00:33:04.670 --> 00:33:10.670
doesn't take place. BOP officials should keep in mind what the Supreme Court said about diesel

00:33:10.670 --> 00:33:18.270
therapy in the case of Frazier v. Dubois. Section 1210 transfers. Although prisoners enjoy no

00:33:18.270 --> 00:33:23.790
constitutional right to remain in a particular institution, prison officials do not have discretion

00:33:23.790 --> 00:33:28.590
to punish an inmate for exercising his First Amendment rights by transferring him to a different

00:33:28.590 --> 00:33:36.190
institution. Frazier v. Dubois, 1990. Similarly, I have a constitutional right against retaliation

00:33:36.190 --> 00:33:42.030
as the Supreme Court set forth in Block v. Rybar and in Scoog v. County of Clackamas.

00:33:42.910 --> 00:33:49.150
Section 460, retaliation. Plaintiffs had a First Amendment right to criticize a public official's

00:33:49.150 --> 00:33:53.550
performance of his duties and in action alleging retaliation by official against

00:33:53.550 --> 00:33:58.270
plaintiffs due to their exercise of their First Amendment rights, it was insufficient for

00:33:58.270 --> 00:34:03.790
them to allege injury in form of embarrassment, humiliation, and emotional distress.

00:34:04.510 --> 00:34:09.710
Right exists to be free of police action for which retaliation is but for cause,

00:34:09.710 --> 00:34:15.630
even if probable cause exists for that action. These cases are freely available in the Prison

00:34:15.630 --> 00:34:20.830
Law Library. Perhaps prison officials should acquaint themselves with them. Maybe they could

00:34:20.830 --> 00:34:27.870
also look up Largent v. Texas, which prohibits censorship. Section 306, censorship.

00:34:28.590 --> 00:34:35.070
Any regulation which makes dissemination of ideas depend upon approval of distributor by official

00:34:35.070 --> 00:34:40.670
constitutes administrative censorship in extreme form and subject to certain exceptions. Any

00:34:40.670 --> 00:34:46.430
regulation which subjects communications to license infringes right of free speech,

00:34:46.430 --> 00:34:53.070
Largent v. Texas. Where do we go from here? First, understand that any monolithic bureaucracy

00:34:53.070 --> 00:34:58.590
will tend toward corruption without proper oversight. There is an internal administrative

00:34:58.590 --> 00:35:04.110
remedy process that's a joke. You write a complaint and they tell you to go screw yourself.

00:35:05.390 --> 00:35:10.910
Calling for an inspector general investigation is also a joke. An inspector general could make an

00:35:10.910 --> 00:35:16.350
entire career investigating where the money from the inmate trust fund goes. Where did that

00:35:16.350 --> 00:35:21.950
new flat screen TV and the CO medical lounge, especially during federal budget sequestration

00:35:22.030 --> 00:35:28.910
come from? The only alternative is to go to the top. BOP director Charles Samuels. Director Samuels

00:35:28.910 --> 00:35:33.630
worked his way up after starting as a line CO, moving up through the ranks to Warden and then

00:35:33.630 --> 00:35:39.230
onto Washington to lead the BOP. Certainly he knows the difference between right and wrong.

00:35:39.230 --> 00:35:43.150
Certainly he wouldn't want his employees to violate the law, as I've documented in these

00:35:43.150 --> 00:35:47.790
letters. Certainly he wouldn't want his people's actions highlighted in a press investigation.

00:35:48.750 --> 00:35:52.430
So join me in writing director Samuels and in demanding an end to these

00:35:52.430 --> 00:35:57.870
illegal and unconstitutional actions by his staff. We have to put our foot down and say

00:35:57.870 --> 00:36:02.190
enough. I'll let you know how things develop. Best regards, John.

00:36:03.790 --> 00:36:07.950
I added a post script to this letter from Loretto. It says this.

00:36:08.670 --> 00:36:13.870
I wanted to thank representative Jim Moran, Democrat of Virginia, who sent a second letter

00:36:13.870 --> 00:36:19.470
to director Samuels last week saying, quote, As you will recall, I sent a letter last September

00:36:19.470 --> 00:36:24.670
requesting that the Department of Justice grant my constituent, John Kiriaku, at least nine months

00:36:24.670 --> 00:36:30.190
of halfway house time. Despite the fact that 12 months of halfway house time is well within BOP

00:36:30.190 --> 00:36:35.550
guidelines, I am disappointed to learn that John's return to society may be unnecessarily

00:36:35.550 --> 00:36:40.590
delayed. Thus, I am writing to reiterate the importance of John's release to a halfway

00:36:40.590 --> 00:36:45.630
house as soon as possible, so that he can be a father to his five children and resume

00:36:45.630 --> 00:36:52.830
productive contributions to society, unquote. Representative Moran is a 12 term congressman

00:36:52.830 --> 00:36:57.870
and a member of the House Appropriations Committee, which controls the BOP budget.

00:36:58.990 --> 00:37:04.430
Addendum about 12 hours after I wrote this letter from Loretto, I was called to the

00:37:04.430 --> 00:37:09.630
special investigative service office. The CEO there handed me an envelope containing the

00:37:09.630 --> 00:37:16.510
first 20,000 words of this book. I hadn't even realized it was missing since the shakedown.

00:37:17.150 --> 00:37:22.350
The SIS CEO said that the CIO who had shaken me down had determined that the manuscript

00:37:22.350 --> 00:37:29.550
had, quote, made threats against staff, unquote. He said he too had read it and believed that

00:37:29.550 --> 00:37:34.990
it did not contain any threats to staff. The allegation was patently absurd in any event.

00:37:34.990 --> 00:37:39.230
He returned it to me in its entirety, although he almost certainly made a copy.

00:37:40.590 --> 00:37:44.750
In one last swipe at my civil rights and my constitutional right to freedom of speech,

00:37:44.750 --> 00:37:51.390
the shakedown CEO tried to remove my desk from the wall and to confiscate it. After all, if I

00:37:51.390 --> 00:37:56.750
have no desk, I can't write letters from Loretto, right? After a while he gave up,

00:37:56.750 --> 00:38:02.190
the bolts were stripped and wouldn't budge. I had stripped them on purpose as a preemptive

00:38:02.190 --> 00:38:07.070
measure. It was a temporary respite though. The CEO issued a work order to chip it

00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:12.830
off the wall. I had to go to the unit manager who promised me that the desk would not be removed.

00:38:13.950 --> 00:38:20.190
It wasn't. These crude, amateurish attempts to deprive me of my rights don't originate with a

00:38:20.190 --> 00:38:25.150
low-level CEO. They come from higher up, from officials who should know better. But I have

00:38:25.150 --> 00:38:30.190
the Constitution in my corner and I won't stop fighting. After my letter was published,

00:38:30.190 --> 00:38:33.630
I taped a page from a legal pad on the desk and I wrote on it,

00:38:33.630 --> 00:38:40.510
This desk kills fascism. This was a play on this machine kills fascism, which folksinger Woody Guthrie

00:38:40.510 --> 00:38:45.950
had famously written on his guitar in the 1930s. The sign hung up on the desk for only a couple of

00:38:45.950 --> 00:38:50.750
hours before a CEO tore it down, crumpled it into a ball, and threw it on the floor.

00:38:51.550 --> 00:38:56.830
I picked it up and mailed it home to myself. I keep it as a reminder that I was not alone

00:38:56.830 --> 00:39:02.030
as I went through this experience. Outside Loretto, America was beginning to more fully

00:39:02.030 --> 00:39:06.190
reckon with the terrible things that had been done on our collective behalf.

00:39:06.190 --> 00:39:12.190
The Senate is notoriously deliberative and slow. But as I fought the corruption inherent in my

00:39:12.190 --> 00:39:16.430
punishment, the US Senate was about to address the corruption that punished me.

00:39:17.150 --> 00:39:21.710
Remember that famous Nietzsche quote I referenced a few episodes back about staring into the

00:39:21.710 --> 00:39:27.550
abyss and becoming the monster? Well the good news was I could almost begin to see the

00:39:27.550 --> 00:39:32.990
light at the end of this Godforsaken tunnel and for a change it wasn't an oncoming train.

00:39:33.710 --> 00:39:39.630
But what had survival cost me inside my head? Inside my soul? We've got so much more story

00:39:39.630 --> 00:39:45.550
to tell in the episodes ahead. We will get into the Senate's report on torture. It doesn't turn

00:39:45.550 --> 00:39:50.990
out well for the CIA. But in the next two episodes we're going to talk about rules

00:39:50.990 --> 00:39:56.110
and about food. Breaking the rules in prison and strangest part of all enjoying

00:39:56.190 --> 00:40:02.510
some of the food there, all while doing time like a spy. Until next time, I'm John Kiriakou.

